tax loss harvesting often said to be a  silver lining in a down Market  here's how it works when your  Investments go south you can sell them  from your brokerage account at a loss  and then use that loss to reduce your  tax bill in the US once your losses  exceed capital gains you can subtract up  to three thousand dollars per year from  ordinary income and if your losses  exceed three thousand that can be  carried forward to offset games in  future years that's some damage control  for portfolios in a bruising year in  which both stocks and bonds have  declined taxos harvesting could even  make the crypto crash a little less  painful crypto investors have  collectively lost trillions of dollars  since digital coins heat but they may  have a special tax advantage stock  owners have to follow What's called the  wash sale rule if they sell a stock for  a loss they have to wait 30 days before  buying the same security again or else  it won't be eligible for a deduction so  far the IRS has not said this wash cell  wall applied to digital assets still  some tax experts warn crypto investors  could get burnt by the irs's economic  substance doctrine that will basically  says that you can't do something just  for a tax benefit and if you plan on  selling crypto at a loss make sure you  know how long you've been holding your  coins anything under the one year mark  is considered a short-term capital loss  short-term losses will be used to offset  short-term gains first and then  long-term gains whilst this strategy  won't completely ease the sting of  crypto losses it may provide some relief  happy harvesting  [Music]
 

